From 07ff8d1d4df43876eccb1daaa8c7c159c0f1315d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 18:10:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Phase 11 patch 0061 -- wave-50 cycle 1 VRAM-resident
 page-flip helper

Cycle 1 of the multi-wave VRAM-resident render pivot per
docs/internal/WAVE-50-VRAM-RESIDENT-RENDER-DESIGN.md. LOAD-BEARING
DIAGNOSTIC, not an fps lever -- this cycle answers whether VRAM writes
(LFB nearptr or banked dosmemput to off-screen pages) escape the
PODP83 sysmem 20 MB/s bandwidth ceiling that probe-engineer's wave-50 v0
verdict identified as structural. If they do, the multi-cycle pivot
proceeds (cycle 2 repoints engine surface; cycle 3 reanimates Cirrus
BLT); if they don't, KPI retargets to ~30 fps per WAVE-49 sec. 7.

Three new public APIs in include/SDL3/SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h:

  #define SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_VRAM_RESIDENT "SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_VRAM_RESIDENT"
  bool SDL_DOSVesaGetBackBufferPage(const SDL_DOSVesaDirectState *st,
                                     int page_idx, Uint8 **out_nearptr,
                                     int *out_pitch);
  bool SDL_DOSVesaPagePresent(const SDL_DOSVesaDirectState *st, int page_idx);

The killswitch hint is strict-"1" match per CLAUDE.md DOSKUTSU env-var
convention: default OFF for cycle 1 (load-bearing diagnostic ships
default-OFF per [[author_flagged_caveat_overrides_let_data_decide]]);
flips to default-ON after cycle 2 validates fps gain.

Encoding anchor: tests/probes/crtcswap.c verdict at
docs/internal/WAVE-50-CRTCSWAP-PROBE-RESULTS.md sec. 3 confirmed
BYTE-units encoding for CRTC[0x0C/0x0D] on g2k Cirrus 5434 + UniVBE 6.70
in VBE 8bpp linear modes; CRTC[0x1B] bit 0 carries display-start bit 16
for offsets >= 65536. The 76800-byte page-1 offset fits in 17 bits via
0x0C/0x0D + 0x1B bit 0. Helper defensively programs CRTC[0x1D] bits
6:7 for bits 17:18 even though pages 0..1 don't need them, so the
register state stays deterministic across page toggles.

Strict Cirrus 5434 detection (CRTC[0x27] == 0xA8) reuses SDL/0060's
SDL_DOSVesaDirect_IsCirrusBLTAvailable() probe -- same chip-rev anchor,
same killswitch composition (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_CIRRUS_BLT=0 also
disables this helper because the probe was verified only on Cirrus 5434).
Other Cirrus variants (5430/5436/5446) and non-Cirrus VESA chips fall
through to "not available" since the encoding probe verified only on
5434 + UniVBE 6.7.

Runtime encoding sanity check per probe-engineer recommendation:

  - CRTC[0x14] bit 6 (Underline Location, double-word mode flag) --
    if set, abort engagement with a WARN banner; the probe verified
    only byte-units encoding, so dword addressing is a clearly
    disqualifying configuration.
  - CRTC[0x17] bit 6 (Mode Control, word/byte mode flag) -- logged
    for diagnostic visibility but NOT used to gate engagement (VGA
    bit polarity varies across implementations; safe default is to
    trust the probe-verified byte path unless dword is configured).
  - SR[0x07] (Cirrus extended display mode) -- logged for diagnostic
    visibility only.

Divert mechanism in SDL_DOSVesaDirectPresentFull:

  - Pre-divert path (default-OFF): identical to pre-patch behavior;
    LFB SDL_memcpy / banked dosmemput / BankedDosmemput at
    st->page_offset (=0 in current build).
  - Divert path (VRAM_RESIDENT=1 + chip OK + sanity OK):
    1. Compute back-page = 1 - visible_page; back_offset = back * fb_size.
    2. Write pixels to back_offset via LFB SDL_memcpy or banked
       BankedDosmemput (single-bank dosmemput cannot reach the
       offset-76800 back-page because it crosses the 64 KB bank
       boundary -- force the multi-bank walker).
    3. CRTC swap to back_offset via direct programming of CRTC[0x0D]
       (low), CRTC[0x0C] (high), CRTC[0x1B] bit 0 (bit-16 extension),
       and CRTC[0x1D] bits 6:7 (bits 17:18 extension; defensively
       cleared for pages 0/1).
    4. WaitForVBlank() (existing primitive at SDL_dosframebuffer.c:1098)
       before CRTC programming so the swap takes effect at the next
       frame boundary instead of mid-scan (tear-free).
    5. Toggle visible_page_idx so the NEXT present writes to the
       OTHER page.

Engagement-flag decoupled from back-page-offset value: the back-page
byte offset is LEGITIMATELY 0 when the visible page is page 1
(back = page 0 = offset 0). The compute helper returns a bool
"engaged" plus an out-pointer for the offset, so callers cannot
mistakenly disengage the divert based on offset==0.

doskutsu_dbg_log banners (smoke-gate two-witness pattern):

  - "sdl: wave-50 VRAM-resident page-flip ENABLED (back-page=0x012C00;
    CRTC encoding=BYTE verified via probe; CRTC[0x14]=0xXX CRTC[0x17]=
    0xXX SR[0x07]=0xXX)" on successful first engagement.
  - "sdl: wave-50 VRAM-resident page-flip DISABLED (chip not Cirrus
    5434 OR ...)" on non-5434 fallback.
  - "sdl: wave-50 VRAM-resident page-flip DISABLED (chip configured
    for non-byte encoding: CRTC[0x14]=0xXX bit6=1 (dword); ...
    UNEXPECTED -- file probe-engineer follow-up)" on sanity-check
    fail.
  - "sdl: wave-50 VRAM-resident page-flip first swap (back_page_
    byte_offset=0x000000; visible_page now=1)" once on first
    successful divert + swap (runtime-witness for the two-witness
    smoke gate).

Per CLAUDE.md sec. Critical Rules:
  - Strict-match env-var per DOSKUTSU convention.
  - ASCII-only source text.
  - "DOSKUTSU patch 0061" block comment for attribution; no DOS-PORT
    tag (this is SDL3-DOS-backend-native code, not port glue).

No engine code touched -- cycle 1 mechanism is "SDL CRTC-page-flip
primitive + VRAM-back-page write divert + runtime encoding sanity
check". Cycle 2 (nx-engine surface repointing) ships separately if
the cycle-1 diagnostic validates the LFB-bandwidth assumption.

Workspace-local patch (per sdl_ai_policy memory + this repo's
vendor/SDL/CLAUDE.md notice: AI-authored SDL patches stay local,
never contributed back).

Modifies:
  include/SDL3/SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h  (new API + hint name decl)
  src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c       (divert + helpers + statics)

Engine-side integration (cycle 2) + smoke-gate BANNERS array update
+ docs/internal/BOOT.md entry live in the parent doskutsu repo (not
in this vendor commit).
